[US] usc_78i: Securities Exchange Act Section 9(a) — 15 U.S.C. 78i (wash trades, matched orders, manipulative series)
    https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/USCODE-2023-title15/html/USCODE-2023-title15-chap2B-sec78i.htm
    checked_on=2026-11-10 effective_from=see source status=compared with current US Code through PL 119-138 (uscode.house.gov /us/usc/119-138/t15/s78i/): §78i(a) matches the 2023 edition; last amendment 2010 (PL 111-203)
    summary: 9(a)(1): no-change-in-beneficial-ownership trades / matched orders to create a false appearance of active trading; 9(a)(2): series of transactions to induce others. Wash TRADE (manipulation) != wash SALE (tax). Not legal advice.
[US] finra_5210: FINRA Rule 5210 Supplementary Material .02 (self-trades) and .03 (disruptive quoting and trading)
    https://www.finra.org/rules-guidance/rulebooks/finra-rules/5210
    checked_on=2026-11-10 effective_from=2017-04-03 (SR-FINRA-2017-004) status=in force per source text on checked_on
    summary: Unintentional self-trades generally bona fide, but firms must review for and prevent a pattern from a single or related algorithms; .03 Type 1 (layer one side, trade other side, cancel) and Type 2 (inside-NBBO order, trade against joiners); cross-venue patterns count.
[US] sec_2026_37_cat_review: SEC press release 2026-37 — concept release on the Consolidated Audit Trail (CAT) review
    https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/press-releases/2026-37-sec-seeks-public-comment-consolidated-audit-trail-other-audit-trails-data-sources
    checked_on=2026-11-10 effective_from=n/a status=concept release (2026-04-16); review not concluded
    summary: Comprehensive review of CAT (funding/cost, regulatory purpose, structure/governance, design/scope). CAT exists under Rule 613 (adopted 2012-07-11). Do not predict the outcome.
[US] sec_34_106402_innovation_exemption: SEC Release 34-106402 (File 4-927) — Innovation Exemption order: TSVs exempt from 'exchange', Covered Firms from 'dealer' (tokenized NMS stock)
    https://www.sec.gov/files/rules/exorders/2026/34-106402.pdf
    checked_on=2026-11-10 effective_from=2026-09-17 status=temporary conditional exemptive order; effective 2026-09-17 until 2031-09-17 (section V); 91 FR 60168 (2026-09-22); no comment closing date set, SEC still accepting comments on checked_on
    summary: Section 36(a)(1) exemptions. Conditions incl. symbol/volume limits by LULD tier (Tier 1: 75 symbols, 0.25% of that stock's prior-month ADV; Tier 2: 250 symbols, 2.5%), same rights as traditional stock, synthetics excluded, issuer notice/objection for third-party tokens, public auditable smart contracts on a public permissionless ledger, halt with primary listing exchange, USD transaction data (UTC times), TSV not subject to Reg NMS. Not a final rule; no venue recommended; not legal advice.
[US] sec_atkins_innovation_exemption_2026: Chairman Atkins — Statement on the Innovation Exemption (2026-09-17)
    https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/speeches-statements/atkins-innovation-exemption-bridge-toward-durable-rulemaking-091726
    checked_on=2026-11-10 effective_from=n/a status=commissioner statement (explains the order; not the order itself)
    summary: Key conditions as stated: TSV must be a U.S. person and comply with OFAC sanctions; permissioned access; no synthetics, tokens carry the same rights incl. dividends and voting; issuers can object. Anti-fraud/anti-manipulation provisions apply in full.
[US] sec_uyeda_innovation_exemption_2026: Commissioner Uyeda — Statement on the Innovation Exemption (2026-09-17)
    https://www.sec.gov/newsroom/speeches-statements/uyeda-statement-innovation-exemption-091726
    checked_on=2026-11-10 effective_from=n/a status=commissioner statement (explains the order; not the order itself)
    summary: Symbol limits and volume caps calibrated by LULD tiers; USD transaction data (price, size, time, pool address, end-of-day pool size, daily volume) public at regular intervals.
